WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:21.622
The small man cub sat in the circle with the wolf cubs.

2
00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:26.500
He was playing with some white pebbles that glowed in the moonlight.

3
00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:34.104
Father Wolf nudged Mowgli forward with his nose.

4
00:00:34.105 --> 00:00:41.055
"Look well, oh, wolves!" Akela cried, as he'd done with the other cubs.

5
00:00:41.056 --> 00:00:49.215
Before any wolves could respond, a muffled roar came from behind the rocks.

6
00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:53.681
It was Shere Khan.

7
00:00:53.682 --> 00:00:58.094
"The cub is mine!" the tiger growled.

8
00:00:58.095 --> 00:01:02.234
"Give him to me!"

9
00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:06.456
"Look well, oh, wolves!" Akela called.

10
00:01:06.457 --> 00:01:11.190
"Look well upon this cub!"

11
00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:17.419
The law of the jungle was that two wolves had to speak for the cub.

12
00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.778
This was how the pack accepted the wolf cubs.

13
00:01:21.779 --> 00:01:26.295
"Who will speak for this cub?" Akela called.

14
00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:31.092
Mother Wolf tensed, ready to defend Mowgli.

15
00:01:31.093 --> 00:01:34.687
Akela was still waiting for someone to speak.

16
00:01:34.688 --> 00:01:42.390
Besides the wolves in the pack, only one other animal was allowed at the pack council.

17
00:01:42.391 --> 00:01:49.616
It was Baloo, a sleepy brown bear who taught the wolf cubs the law of the jungle.

18
00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:57.246
Baloo ate only nuts, roots, and honey, so none of the other jungle creatures feared him.

19
00:01:57.247 --> 00:02:02.782
As Shere Khan stepped closer, the brown bear rose on his back legs.

20
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:07.252
He grunted loudly. "I speak for the human cub.

21
00:02:07.253 --> 00:02:09.615
Let him run with the pack.

22
00:02:09.616 --> 00:02:14.262
I will teach him, as I teach the other cubs."

23
00:02:14.263 --> 00:02:19.688
"Who else will speak for the human cub?" Akela called.

24
00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:24.719
Just then a black shadow dropped down into the circle.

25
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.419
It was Bagheera, the black panther.

26
00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.789
The wolves quickly backed away from him.

27
00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:35.800
"Akela, I have no right to be here."

28
00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:41.046
The black panther's voice was as soft as honey dripping from a tree.

29
00:02:41.047 --> 00:02:47.452
"But the law of the jungle says a cub's life may be bought. Am I right?"

30
00:02:47.453 --> 00:02:51.868
"Yes!" a few young wolves replied eagerly.

31
00:02:51.869 --> 00:02:54.932
The young wolves were always hungry.

32
00:02:54.933 --> 00:03:00.064
"Akela!" one wolf called. "Listen to Bagheera.

33
00:03:00.065 --> 00:03:05.853
The cub can be bought for a price. It is the law of the jungle."

34
00:03:05.854 --> 00:03:09.216
The black panther smiled gently.

35
00:03:09.217 --> 00:03:15.359
"I'd like to propose a deal. Baloo has already spoken for the boy.

36
00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.748
If the rest of you accept him, I will share some delicious food with you.

37
00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:25.638
It's a fat bull, freshly killed."

38
00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:28.034
Mother Wolf looked at Father.

39
00:03:28.035 --> 00:03:33.661
"Why is the panther speaking up for Mowgli?" she said. Father shrugged.

40
00:03:33.662 --> 00:03:37.972
The other wolves had gathered to discuss the situation.

41
00:03:37.973 --> 00:03:42.820
"The boy will die in the winter rains," one said.

42
00:03:42.821 --> 00:03:46.458
"He will burn in the sun," another added.

43
00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:50.172
"What harm can a little cub do?"

44
00:03:50.173 --> 00:03:54.004
"Come on. Let's let him run with the pack."

45
00:03:54.005 --> 00:03:57.991
Finally the wolves agreed to accept Mowgli.

46
00:03:57.992 --> 00:04:02.117
Mowgli sat calmly, playing with the white pebbles.

47
00:04:02.118 --> 00:04:06.083
Akela's cry rose as they each inspected him.

48
00:04:06.084 --> 00:04:10.101
"Look well—look well, wolves!"

49
00:04:10.102 --> 00:04:16.518
Soon the pack started down the hill to eat the meal promised by the panther.

50
00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:22.503
Akela, Bagheera, Baloo, and Mowgli's family stayed behind at the rock.

51
00:04:22.504 --> 00:04:28.114
With a furious roar, Shere Khan stalked away from them.

52
00:04:28.115 --> 00:04:32.378
"Roar all you want, tiger," Bagheera muttered.

53
00:04:32.379 --> 00:04:35.801
"I have a feeling about this man cub.

54
00:04:35.802 --> 00:04:42.351
One day Mowgli will make you roar for another reason, Shere Khan."

55
00:04:42.352 --> 00:04:46.940
Akela turned to Mother and Father Wolf with a smile.

56
00:04:46.941 --> 00:04:54.132
"Humans are very wise. Perhaps your man cub can help our pack in some way."

57
00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:57.101
Mowgli's parents nodded their thanks.

58
00:04:57.102 --> 00:05:01.337
Then Father Wolf turned to the bear.

59
00:05:01.338 --> 00:05:04.809
"And thank you for your help today, Baloo.

60
00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:09.265
Please begin training little Mowgli as soon as possible.

61
00:05:09.266 --> 00:05:22.804
He must learn how to be a wolf."
